        "# NGO Connect – ML Engine\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. Business Understanding\n",
        "\n",
        "**The problem:** In Nairobi, many people want to volunteer but do not know which NGO or cause suits them, and NGOs struggle to find volunteers with the right skills. Matching is currently done by hand or by chance.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What the ML engine does:** A volunteer enters their skills, availability and location. The engine predicts which type of organisation (cause area) suits them best, and shows why.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Type of ML problem:** This is a *classification* problem. The model learns from past examples (volunteers whose best-fit cause is known) and then predicts the cause area for a new volunteer.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Success measure:** The model should predict the right cause area for volunteers it has not seen before, and give a reason that a normal user can understand.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Where it fits in the app:** The mobile app sends the volunteer's details to the engine, and the engine returns the recommended cause areas."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UOZn-c9jBDHM"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Key Terms\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Feature:** a piece of information the model uses, such as a volunteer's skills.\n",
        "- **Target:** what we want to predict. Here it is the cause area (Type of Organization).\n",
        "- **Classification:** predicting which group something belongs to, like which cause area suits a volunteer.\n",
        "- **Training and test set:** the training volunteers teach the model, and the test volunteers are kept hidden to check it on people it has not seen.\n",
        "- **Accuracy:** the share of test volunteers that get the correct cause area.\n",
        "- **Cross-validation:** testing the model several times, each time on a different part of the training data, then averaging the scores.\n",
        "- **Confidence:** how sure the model is about a cause area, shown as a percentage."
      ],
