      "source": [
        "## 4. Data Preparation\n",
        "\n",
        "A model can only work with numbers, so the columns need converting first.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Columns removed:** Volunteer Name and Gender. A name says nothing about which cause suits someone, and gender should not influence who gets matched to what. Age is also removed, because in this data it has no link to the cause area, and age should not decide where someone volunteers.\n",
        "- **Skills (text):** converted with **TF-IDF**. This gives each word a score based on how important it is: words that appear in many volunteers' skills (like \"community\") score lower, and words that appear in fewer (like \"veterinary\") score higher.\n",
        "- **Availability and Location (categories):** converted with **one-hot encoding**. Each option becomes its own column with 1 (yes) or 0 (no).\n",
        "- **Train/test split:** 80% of the volunteers are used to teach the model and 20% are kept hidden to test it. This shows how it handles volunteers it has never seen."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mcw6wus6NxzM"
      }
