        "## 6. Modelling\n",
        "\n",
        "I compare three classification algorithms that suit text and category data:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Logistic Regression:** gives each word and category a weight for each cause area, adds them up, and picks the cause with the highest score. It is simple and easy to explain.\n",
        "- **Naive Bayes:** works out how likely each cause area is given the skills a volunteer has, assuming each skill counts independently. It is fast and works well on small text data.\n",
        "- **Random Forest:** builds many decision trees that each vote on the cause area, and the most popular answer wins. It handles more complex patterns but is harder to explain.\n",
        "\n",
        "To compare them fairly, I use **5-fold cross-validation** on the training data only. The training set is split into 5 parts, and each part takes a turn as a mini test set while the model learns from the other 4. The scores are then averaged. The real test set stays hidden until the final check."
